+## Context
+
+Tasks are built by `createTask` and changed by pure functions in `src/domain/task.ts`, orchestrated by `createTaskList` in `src/domain/list.ts`. Domain code never throws and returns a `Result`. Titles are trimmed on `add` and `rename`.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:**
+- Clear, specific errors for the four kinds of bad input, with no side effects on rejection.
+
+**Non-Goals:**
+- Validating `untag`, `find` or other lookups; normalising tags; changing the trimming of titles.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Add error code `invalid-input` to `TodoErrorCode`.
+- Add validators in `task.ts` (`validateTitle`, `validatePriority`, `validateTag`), each returning a `Result`, with TSDoc. The title is trimmed first; the 120-character limit applies to the trimmed title. A tag is rejected if empty or if it contains any whitespace character.
+- `add` validates title, priority and every tag before reading the clock, issuing an id or storing. `rename` and `tag` validate their argument before looking up the task, so bad input is reported even for an unknown task. Validation precedes the duplicate check.
+- Priority is checked at runtime against `PRIORITIES`, since screens pass untyped text.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- A new error code may surprise exhaustive matches on `TodoErrorCode`.
