+## Why
+
+Some screens pass whatever the user typed straight to the list, so odd tasks get in: blank or huge titles, unknown priorities, tags that are empty or hold spaces. The list must refuse such input with a clear error.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- `add`, `rename` and `tag` reject invalid input with a new `invalid-input` error whose message says what is wrong:
+  - a title that is empty or only spaces;
+  - a title longer than 120 characters (after trimming);
+  - a priority other than `low`, `normal` or `high`;
+  - a tag that is empty or contains a space (for `add`, any of its tags).
+- A rejected call changes nothing in the list: no task added, renamed or tagged, no id consumed, no `updatedAt` change.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+- `task-list`: `add`, `rename` and `tag` validate their input.
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/domain/result.ts` (new error code), `src/domain/task.ts`, `src/domain/list.ts`, `test/list.test.ts`.
+- Callers that matched on `TodoErrorCode` see one more code. No new dependency.
